Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:10:46 +0100
Subject: [M156] [ic] Fix the megamorphic cache variant of the
 DefineNamedOwn-inside-class bug
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Original change's description:
> [ic] Fix the megamorphic cache variant of the DefineNamedOwn-inside-class bug
>
> Previous fix: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8501161
>
> Turns out, there's a variant of this bug where the handlers for
> DefineNamedOwn and DefineNamedOwnInLiteral are shared via the
> megamorphic cache.
>
> DefineNamedOwnInLiteral can be made megamorphic like this:
> {__proto__: prototype, value}
>
> Thus, we no longer can decide based on the handler whether we should
> invalidate the constness, but we can decide it based on the call site.
> This way we can still use the same megamorphic cache for the Define
> handlers.
>
> 1) StoreIC::ComputeHandler: Remove the logic that we can store to const
>    fields with kMutable type handlers. Create kConst handlers instead.
>
> 2) AccessorAssembler::HandleStoreFieldAndReturn: When handling
>    DefineNamedOwnInLiteral, allow using kConst handlers without checking
>    the constness of the value.
>
> 3) Wire up "in literal" vs "not in literal" throughout the IC layer. We
>    distinguish based on the bytecode we're handling. Add a StoreICMode
>    for keeping track of that.
>
> TAG=agy
> CONV=6b85f44b-a64d-4597-9836-a71bc2161edf
>
> Fixed: 576439987
> Change-Id: I1aad8f81bdc3c5ddc713c984f8e0d8206023f8b5
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8691330
> Reviewed-by: Igor Sheludko <ishell@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Victor Gomes <victorgomes@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#111587}

(cherry picked from commit df78e0051bb566bcfc9d9dfe931fd86e276a5f32)

Bug: 582139208,576439987
Change-Id: I1aad8f81bdc3c5ddc713c984f8e0d8206023f8b5

Electron adaptation notes (45-x-y):
Taken from the author's pending [M156] rebase (8744094), whose
src/ic/accessor-assembler.cc was uploaded with unresolved conflict markers.
On 15.6, HandleStoreICSmiHandlerCase and HandleStoreFieldAndReturn do not
yet take a StoreICMode (that plumbing and the maybe_initializing_store switch
come from the unrelated main-only change 535c5a6fddb "[objects] Use
UninitializedHeapNumber for uninitialized double fields"), so the mode is
threaded through mechanically here: StoreICParameters::mode() is added, both
helpers gain a StoreICMode parameter, HandleStoreICHandlerCase passes
p->mode(), and the four HandleStoreFieldAndReturn call sites forward it. The
upstream hunk that adds kDefineNamedOwnInLiteral to the
maybe_initializing_store switch has no counterpart on this branch and is
omitted; the branch's existing Float64SilenceNaN handling is kept. The
kDefineNamedOwnInLiteral checks in CheckHeapObjectTypeMatchesDescriptor and
HandleStoreFieldAndReturn, and every other file, are as upstream.

